342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 104 0 R
/E (The lab shows how LangGraph turns an LLM from a single call into a controllable workflow. State carries information between nodes, conditional edges let the model-driven classifier choose a path, tool nodes let the agent act and loop back, and checkpointers with thread identifiers provide conversational memory. The capstone assistant combines these elements with explicit error handling and a safe calculator, and it behaved correctly across all demonstration scenarios. The main weaknesses are in evaluation depth rather than in the graph design: the routing test is small and lenient, and the classifier and fallback logic would benefit from structured output and stricter validation.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
